docs/study/sections/discussion.typ:11:The standardized regressions expose a design issue in the current PROSPER-style selection path. Search co-evolves policy coordinates and objective weights, evaluates candidates on different seeds, and then chooses across scalar score, counterfactual robustness, mastery, transfer, low confusion, and evidence readiness. In a synthetic-only run, counterfactual and evidence-readiness signals are absent or uninformative, and a winner under its search conditions can underperform under a common objective and seed. Production reduces this risk by requiring at least five real learner outcomes before evolution and by rolling back sufficiently large post-evolution regressions in the transactional auto-improvement loop. Those controls are implemented safeguards; they are not evidence that reward hacking or harmful policy drift has been eliminated.
